ule-template.ts`, passed. I did not run `yarn typecheck` to completion.\n\nThe rule applies in the places that handle weekends:\n- **Next date (`shared/schedules.ts`):** `getNextDate` returns the next weekday occurrence, so a daily schedule starting on a weekend now reports the following Monday rather than a date before its start.\n- **Upcoming dates (`server/schedules/app.ts`):** the preview filters out weekend occurrences and still returns the requested number of dates.\n- **Budget templates (`server/budget/schedule-template.ts`):** weekend occurrences of a daily schedule no longer add to the monthly target.\n- **Parsing (`server/rules/rule-utils.ts`):** the schedule data now carries `frequency`.\n\nWeekly, monthly and yearly schedules, and schedules with weekend handling off, behave as before.\n\nIf a daily schedule only ever lands on weekends (for example, every 7 days starting on a Saturday), `getNextDate` returns null. Before this change it would have moved each occurrence to a weekday.\n\nI added tests in `shared/schedules.test.ts` for both directions and for the weekends-only case.","ttft_ms":2259,"type":"result","duration_ms":1298102,"uuid":"16e781dc-0024-435b-b736-c38510d5fab6","ttft_stream_ms":1607,"time_to_request_ms":375,"first_content_frame_ms":1608,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
