 and all in test setup (`updateVersion`). The run took about 1000 seconds because it overlapped with other background jobs. Run alone, `app.test.ts` passes (31 of 31). `shared/schedules.test.ts` passed in an earlier run, and `schedule-template.test.ts` passed in that same combined run, but I did not re-run either alone after the final edits.\n\n- **Next date:** `getNextDate` in `shared/schedules.ts` returns the next weekday occurrence. A daily schedule that starts on a weekend now reports the following Monday instead of a date before its start.\n- **Upcoming dates:** the preview in `server/schedules/app.ts` drops weekend occurrences and still returns the requested number of dates.\n- **Budget templates:** weekend occurrences of a daily schedule no longer add to the monthly target in `server/budget/schedule-template.ts`.\n- **Parsing:** the schedule data now carries `frequency` (`server/rules/rule-utils.ts`).\n\nWeekly, monthly and yearly schedules, and schedules with weekend handling off, behave as before.\n\nIf a daily schedule only ever lands on weekends (for example, every 7 days starting on a Saturday), `getNextDate` now returns null. Before, it moved each occurrence to a weekday.\n\nI added tests for both directions and for the weekends-only case in `shared/schedules.test.ts`.","ttft_ms":2296,"type":"result","duration_ms":40479,"uuid":"bf11640f-bf6b-4bcd-ac7b-1b75d71ed8ee","ttft_stream_ms":1427,"time_to_request_ms":270,"first_content_frame_ms":1428,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":1}
